 the unseeded Nasibov advancing via a tight 7-6 decision."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final was not close as Geraei won gold by technical superiority, ending the match at 4:09 while leading 9-1. El-Sayed had some consolation in taking bronze, but by the narrowest of margins. He met " [:a {:href "/athletes/146291"} "Artyom Surkov"] ", a ROC team member, and only won the match on a judges’ decision after they tied at 1-1. The other bronze went to German " [:a {:href "/athletes/123207"} "Frank Stäbler"] ", who was competing in his third Olympics, but won his first medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Fall", :class "footnote"} "VF"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Technical Superiority", :class "footnote"} "ST"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points Received", :class "footnote"} "TPR"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143836"} "Mohammadreza Geraei"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IRI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IRI.png"}] "IRI"]] [:td {} "14"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "28"] [:td {} "7"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/147082"} "Parviz Nasibov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/UKR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.